2026-10-30T07:40:51.564-07:00 [writer] SENT topic="s0036_drafts" correlation_id="b074e644-966e-4f3d-a7bf-dc3d00b19496" plan=["Identify vulnerable transitive dependency version.", "Determine fix from CVE details.", "Update direct dependency and re-scan."] draft="When a critical CVE affects a transitive dependency, teams must act urgently. First, **identify the vulnerable transitive dependency version** using tools like `npm audit`, `mvn dependency:tree`, or `pip check` to pinpoint the exact package and its version in the dependency chain. Next, **determine the fix** by reviewing the CVE details (e.g., on NVD) to find the required patched version or security update. Crucially, **update the direct dependency** (not just the transitive one) to the fixed version\u2014this breaks the vulnerable chain. Finally, **re-scan the entire dependency graph** post-update to ensure no new critical vulnerabilities were introduced. This targeted approach minimizes risk while maintaining security integrity. (148 words)"
